course: dictionary
lesson: 10093
title: Finding the right word
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A thesaurus is a book or website that groups words with similar meanings. These similar words are called synonyms. Some thesauruses also show words with opposite meanings, called antonyms. You use a thesaurus to find a better or more exact word for your writing.
explain: «Said» is a useful word, but it is plain. A thesaurus might offer «whispered», «shouted» or «muttered». Each one tells the reader something different about how the words were spoken.
explain: Be careful, though. A thesaurus gives words with similar meanings, but not every synonym fits your sentence. Look the new word up in a dictionary, then read your sentence again with it to check that it still makes sense. «You've been arguing with a thesaurus for fifteen minutes» is a joke, but it shows how hard choosing the right word can be.
fact: A thesaurus is a book or website that lists words with similar meanings.
fact: Synonyms are words with similar meanings. Antonyms are words with opposite meanings.
fact: A thesaurus helps you make your writing more interesting and exact.
fact: Synonyms are not always exact matches, so check the meaning in a dictionary before you use a new word.
fact: You can say «look it up in a thesaurus» or «use an online thesaurus».
exercise: What is a thesaurus? | *A book or website that lists words with similar meanings | A map that shows where rivers flow | A book of stories about kings and castles
exercise: Instead of «said», which word could you find in a thesaurus to show the words were spoken quietly? | *whispered | cooked | ran | slept
exercise: Why should you check a synonym in a dictionary before you use it? | Because thesauruses cannot be used at school | Because dictionaries are always wrong | *Because synonyms are not always exact matches | Because it makes the word longer
test: Which word is an antonym of «happy»? | *sad | joyful | glad | cheerful
test: The joke «You've been arguing with a thesaurus for fifteen minutes» suggests what? | Thesauruses are only for numbers | Arguing is the best way to learn new words | A thesaurus is always quick and easy to use | *Choosing the right word can take a long time
exam: Sam wants a better word than «big» for his story. Which word could he find in a thesaurus? | tiny | *enormous | sleepy | happily
